WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.076
- All right, everybody,

00:00:01.076 --> 00:00:01.960
(applause)

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.154
I'm back with Jake Hoot, give it up!

00:00:04.154 --> 00:00:05.890
(cheering)

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:06.810
All right, well, everybody,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.700
we have seen and been horrified

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.890
by the violence against Asian
Americans in our country.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.600
I've always said I wanted this show

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.250
to be a safe place to discuss anything,

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.300
even the tough stuff,
I think it's important,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.380
which is one of the
reasons why I'm honored

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.170
to introduce my next guest.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:26.220
She is an incredibly talented
musician and advocate

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.730
who is using her powerful voice

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.920
to in part express her
emotional experience

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.050
being Asian in America.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.880
You saw her perform at the
Women's March four years ago,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.730
and she recently collaborated
with poet Amanda Gorman,

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.690
who was also on our show.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.973
Please welcome MILCK, everybody!

00:00:44.869 --> 00:00:47.452
(bright music)

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.500
Meet Jake, MILCK!

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.333
- [Jake] Hi!

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.317
- Hi!

00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:53.150
Hi, Jake,

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.330
Hi, Kelly.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.510
- Hello!

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:59.060
But MILCK, you've spoken
out against the recent rise

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.013
in Asian hate crime,

00:01:01.954 --> 00:01:03.490
and you say music has
helped you through this.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.940
I believe music helps people through,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.340
you know, the majority of things,

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.720
I just think it's very
moving and inspiring,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.730
but why personally for you?

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.600
- I grew up using music
as a place of freedom.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.210
I think, you know, I'm a
huge fan of what you do

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.949
and how you sing and how you
bring your own story into it,

00:01:21.949 --> 00:01:26.949
and I don't need to be Asian
enough or American enough

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:30.300
or you know, cool enough in music,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.393
I can just be whoever I am truly,

00:01:34.602 --> 00:01:37.360
and songwriting helps
me explore the topics

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.950
that are difficult to
feel in a (snaps) flash.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.357
I remember hearing this quote.

00:01:43.357 --> 00:01:46.727
"A woman who can sing is
never caged and always free."

00:01:48.224 --> 00:01:51.613
So processing the difficult
and painful moment

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.060
after the Atlanta
shootings and the increase,

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.530
you know, 150% increase of hate crimes

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:02.163
in the US for Asian American hate crimes,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:06.250
this music helps me to put that in a place

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.620
where I can alchemize it

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:13.300
and turn that fear or that
pain into power and purpose,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.390
into love, that's my hope.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.750
- I mean, it's so funny,

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.820
'cause I feel like I'm in Nashville,

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.320
and we're like writers
in the round right now,

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.900
'cause there's three writers

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.194
sitting here right now.

00:02:24.194 --> 00:02:25.027
(Jake laughs)

00:02:25.027 --> 00:02:26.600
And how you just
described how you write is

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.140
how I write with my own life,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.224
and I'm sure that's what you do.

00:02:31.224 --> 00:02:33.029
- Absolutely, that's the
beauty of songwriting.

00:02:33.029 --> 00:02:33.862
- Yeah, it's so therapeutic,

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:35.040
and I love the part that you said

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.290
I process like that too.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.810
I can't, I don't like, like, you know

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.170
when you're like talking with
someone and you're like, look

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.003
I need to step away.

00:02:41.003 --> 00:02:42.990
Cause I don't know exactly
all my thoughts on this.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:43.990
So I just need a minute

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.880
and I go away and writing is
actually very helpful for that.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.260
And I think, you know, also, you know

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:54.000
you being such an advocate
for these important messages

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.870
I think it's important to
use your voice for that.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.900
And your, your writing and it's important

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.050
for you to process that
and you experience that.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:03.883
So it's, you know what I'm saying?

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:04.776
It's people are, it's more believable.

00:03:04.776 --> 00:03:05.609
- Yes.

00:03:05.609 --> 00:03:06.442
- It's authentic.

00:03:06.442 --> 00:03:07.780
It's, it's a beautiful thing.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.960
I think as well, like we've
talked about gender equality

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.630
on the show too, and I
think it ties into, you know

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.150
it can't just be females in that march.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.650
It needs to be men too.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.830
There needs to be men there

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.080
in order for actual change to happen.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.160
And also it can't just be Asians.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.920
There needs to be a diverse group walking

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.330
and marching saying this isn't wrong

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.010
because that's the whole point I feel is

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.180
that nothing's going to change

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.710
unless everybody decides to wake up

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:40.590
and see the issue in order
for that progress to happen.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.930
So I want to talk about your song.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.243
Somebody is beloved.

00:03:45.508 --> 00:03:46.341
So I think I know

00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:48.800
but can you tell everybody,
you know, what inspired it?

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:49.930
- Yes, absolutely.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.080
I wrote this song with
an incredible artist

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.890
Bipolar Sunshine.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.000
This song is inspired by the bravery

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.390
and power that I see with
Tamika Palmer when she speaks

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.140
about her daughter, Breonna Taylor.

00:04:03.995 --> 00:04:06.910
And I, I feel like sometimes the

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.790
the topics can feel really complicated

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.810
but when I zone into the one
human life, cause you know

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.340
we all have been seeing huge numbers of

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.250
of deaths and stuff.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.083
It's hard.

00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.070
And I was like, I think
I'm becoming desensitized

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.730
and I need to just honor a life.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.370
And my hope is, you know

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.250
to bring solidarity between
different communities

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.640
to acknowledge the pain
that we have passed on

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.010
to each other and, and find
ways to move forward together.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.830
And so, you know, we call this

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.460
like a black and gold
conversation coming together

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.780
with black and Asian communities.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.780
And I think that's really
important right now.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.720
And we can be better advocates
for a longer period of time

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.800
if we bring the conversation
to a heart space.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.000
- [Kelly] Agreed. I agree.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.370
Everything from love, speak from love.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.203
I, I agree.

